{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RTgL5tm3TDe2QXq7uHoXCV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a \"Dream\" simulation for their OntoCoDec paper targeting EMNLP 2026 conference main. Let me analyze the current state carefully.\n\nKey context:\n- Target: EMNLP 2026 conference main (4.0 score)\n- Current assessment: 3.5 level, bottleneck is \"novelty incremental, core conclusion intuitively obvious\"\n- Submission deadline: May 25, 2026 (ARR)\n- Several experiments still running: 70B DocRED (unconstrained + constrained), DocRED latency\n\n\n- WikiEvents (EE) cross-task generalization already complete, showing EV/RoV→0% across all models but with residual issues in AC (1.3-3.8%), CF (14.9-21.1%), and increased parse failures\n\nNow I'm thinking through the critical unknowns that will shape the paper's final impact. The 70B experiments are crucial — if larger models still exhibit violations, that strengthens the claim that these aren't just artifacts of smaller models but systematic issues. WikiEvents results are in, showing the pattern holds across tasks but with some complications in certain categories. The real question is whether the narrative can overcome the intuitive obviousness of the core finding.\n\nThe non-obvious elements that could push this toward a stronger contribution are the 70B violations persisting, the extreme discard rate in post-hoc extraction, the dependency chain from grammar to semantics, the non-rectangular structure of the constraint space, and how fallback frequency accounts for remaining violations. The paper's tier depends on what the remaining 70B DocRED results show and whether reviewers buy the cross-task story as a universal framework rather than task-specific observations.\n\nIn the best scenario, those 70B results confirm violations scale with model size and OntoCoDec fixes them, the cross-task experiments feel like a genuine framework contribution, and the non-obvious findings are framed compellingly enough to overcome \"incremental\" pushback. In the middle ground, 70B results are messier, reviewers want more tasks tested, and some still see constrained decoding as obvious—requiring stronger framing of the specific insights and accepting that the CF tradeoff might draw criticism. The worst case is if 70B shows minimal baseline violations that undermine the core motivation.\n\nNow I'm looking at the specific metrics to understand what 70B DocRED might show. The 8B models have substantial violation rates on DocRED, but 70B SciERC is already quite clean, so there's real uncertainty about whether the larger model will still exhibit enough violations to make the systematic study compelling. Now I'm identifying the key metrics I need to track to evaluate this approach—the 70B model's violation reduction on DocRED, how reviewers perceive the novelty of the findings, whether the method generalizes across tasks, how severe the constrained decoding tradeoff appears, and the overall paper reception. Let me structure this with a YAML configuration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":46572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0cab41c-926a-407c-8202-93b8af091189","uuid":"8901caa6-9fd3-4f3b-9c15-5bd1d653a1a3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RTgL5tm3TDe2QXq7uHoXCV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"所有在途实验确认核心假设；非显然发现充分突出；cross-task story 使审稿人认为这是 universal framework 而非 IE-specific trick\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"70B DocRED unconstrained DR ≥8%：大模型仍有系统性违规，否定 'scale solves it' 反驳\"\n      - \"70B DocRED constrained DR ≤2%：OntoCoDec 在 70B 上同样有效\"\n      - \"WikiEvents cross-task + 70B cross-scale 双轴泛化让审稿人接受 'universal framework' framing\"\n      - \"Enabling dependency + tightness×RV interaction + fallback frequency 三个非显然 finding 被审稿人明确标注为 surprising\"\n      - \"CF tradeoff 被接受为 inherent limitation（type system ambiguity 论证成功）\"\n      - \"Post-hoc EE 99.6% discard 作为 killer comparison 有效消除 'just filter' 替代方案\"\n    number_ranges:\n      70b_docred_uncon_DR_pct: [8.0, 15.0]\n      70b_docred_full_s1_DR_pct: [0.5, 2.0]\n      70b_docred_DR_reduction_pct: [85, 95]\n      70b_docred_R_F1_delta_pp: [-0.3, 0.5]\n      cross_task_violation_types_eliminated: [3, 3]  # EV, RoV, ET all → 0%\n      expected_reviewer_avg_score: [3.75, 4.25]\n      novelty_score_avg: [3.5, 4.0]\n      soundness_score_avg: [3.75, 4.25]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Original framing 完全成立：OntoCoDec 是首个 universal ontology-constrained structured generation framework，\n      跨 2 任务（RE+EE）× 4 模型（8B×3 + 70B）× 3 数据集验证。Core claims 无需调整：\n      (1) violation landscape 是独立贡献（70B 仍有 6.5-15% DR 彻底否定 scale-solves-it）；\n      (2) 两层 enabling dependency 是 architecture novelty（非 trivial AND）；\n      (3) tightness×RV baseline 交互作为 deep insight 支撑 §5 analysis；\n      (4) EE post-hoc 99.6% discard 是 devastating comparison。\n      Title 可升级回 \"universal\" 或 \"task-agnostic\"。CF 作为 well-characterized limitation 不会被扣分。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"70B 结果可用但不够亮眼；cross-task story 被接受但审稿人要求更多 task；1-2 个非显然 finding 未充分 land\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"70B DocRED unconstrained DR 3-8%：violations 存在但明显低于 8B，'70B still violates' 说服力打折\"\n      - \"70B DocRED constrained DR ≤1.5%：reduction 有效但绝对改善幅度小（3-6pp），不如 8B dramatic\"\n      - \"审稿人认可 WikiEvents 但提出 'only 2 tasks, need NER/slot-filling etc.' 的 limitation\"\n      - \"Enabling dependency 被理解，但 tightness×RV 交互被视为 dataset-specific observation 而非 general insight\"\n      - \"CF tradeoff 被 1 位审稿人标记为 weakness（'trades one violation type for another'）\"\n      - \"Post-hoc comparison 有效但审稿人指出 'low F1 regime 下 post-hoc 反而更好'（已有数据支撑）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      70b_docred_uncon_DR_pct: [3.0, 8.0]\n      70b_docred_full_s1_DR_pct: [0.3, 1.5]\n      70b_docred_DR_reduction_pct: [70, 90]\n      70b_docred_R_F1_delta_pp: [-0.5, 0.3]\n      cross_task_violation_types_eliminated: [2, 3]  # EV+RoV→0%, AC residual flagged\n      expected_reviewer_avg_score: [3.25, 3.75]\n      novelty_score_avg: [3.0, 3.5]\n      soundness_score_avg: [3.5, 4.0]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      部分假设未完全验证，需 3 处调整：\n      (1) 70B section 降级为 \"violations persist at scale but diminish\" — 不再作为 core evidence，\n      改为 §5.5 补充实验，强调 \"even reduced violations matter for compliance-critical applications\"；\n      (2) Cross-task claim 从 \"universal framework\" 软化为 \"generalizable framework validated on two \n      structurally distinct IE tasks\"，明确 future work 列出 NER/slot-filling/SRL；\n      (3) 将 tightness×RV 交互从 insight 降级为 §5 中的 quantitative analysis，\n      把叙事重心转到 enabling dependency + decidability taxonomy 这两个更 reviewable 的点上。\n      CF tradeoff 需要增加 beam search 作为 mitigation（已有 k=4 消除 DR+CF 的数据），\n      将 beam 从 appendix 提升到正文 §5.5 作为 practical recommendation。\n      目标：Findings accept 有把握，main borderline — 需 rebuttal 期强有力回应。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"70B 几乎无违规（scale 确实 solves it）；novelty incremental 评价未改善；CF 被视为严重缺陷\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"70B DocRED unconstrained DR <3%：审稿人认为 'violations are a small-model problem, method is solving a non-problem at scale'\"\n      - \"70B constrained 无法展示 meaningful reduction（baseline 太低，absolute Δ <2pp）\"\n      - \"审稿人 2/3 仍标记 'novelty incremental'：constrained decoding for IE 被视为 engineering contribution\"\n      - \"Cross-task story 被 dismiss：'same mask logic, different schema config — this is a software feature not a research contribution'\"\n      - \"CF 15-21% 在 EE 上被标记为 'method introduces more problems than it solves'\"\n      - \"F1 too low 攻击面无法完全化解：即使 zero-shot 解释合理，审稿人仍质疑 practical relevance\"\n    number_ranges:\n      70b_docred_uncon_DR_pct: [0.5, 3.0]\n      70b_docred_full_s1_DR_pct: [0.0, 0.5]\n      70b_docred_DR_reduction_pct: [50, 85]\n      70b_docred_R_F1_delta_pp: [-0.3, 0.1]\n      cross_task_violation_types_eliminated: [2, 3]\n      expected_reviewer_avg_score: [2.75, 3.25]\n      novelty_score_avg: [2.5, 3.0]\n      soundness_score_avg: [3.25, 3.75]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      核心 framing 需要重构，但不降级 venue target。三个 reframe 策略（按优先级）：\n      (A) **Violation Landscape as Primary Contribution**：将 §3 violation landscape study \n      升级为论文主体贡献（first systematic measurement + tightness theory + cross-task taxonomy），\n      OntoCoDec 降级为 \"validation that identified violations are addressable\"。\n      这把论文从 \"method paper with empirical validation\" 转为 \"empirical study with method validation\"，\n      novelty 来自 measurement 而非 method。70B 低违规反而变成 positive finding（\"scale partially mitigates \n      but task complexity determines violation severity — EE 64-89% RoV regardless of model size\"）。\n      (B) **Decidability Taxonomy as Theoretical Contribution**：将 prefix-decidability 分类 \n      从 §4 一段扩展为独立 section，formalize 为 theorem（哪些 ontology constraints 可在 autoregressive \n      decoding中 enforce），CF 作为 category (c) 的 concrete evidence 而非 limitation。\n      连接 constrained decoding theory 文献（Willard & Louf 2023, Geng et al. 2024）。\n      (C) **FT composability 作为 practical selling point**：SFT 场景下 DR 0.76%→0.01%（Qwen DocRED），\n      R_F1 保持甚至微升。Frame as \"even well-trained models benefit from decoding-time type checking \n      — analogous to static typing for neural generation\"。这个 angle 对 industry reviewers 有吸引力。\n      三个策略可组合使用。目标仍是 conference main，但需 rebuttal 期全面回应 + AC meta-review 争取。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":46572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0cab41c-926a-407c-8202-93b8af091189","uuid":"27ddaf88-9fb7-4f22-8335-0156473ae39e"}
